{"jivikopanisadavOpamye": [{"id": "jIvikopanizadAvOpamye", "headword": "जीविकोपनिषदावौपम्ये", "headword_slp1": "jIvikopanizadAvOpamye", "fold": "jivikopanisadavOpamye", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The words जीविका and उपनिषद् followed by the verb कृ are called गति when used in the sense of 'likeness and resemblance'.\n\nTerms: गति-प्रध्वम्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["जीविकोपनिषदावौपम्ये १.४.७९", "१.४.७९", "१.४.७९ जीविकोपनिषदावौपम्ये"], "synonyms_slp1": ["jIvikopanizadAvOpamye १.४.७९", "१.४.७९", "१.४.७९ jIvikopanizadAvOpamye"]}], "jivati tu vansye yuva": [{"id": "jIvati tu vaMSye yuvA", "headword": "जीवति तु वंश्ये युवा", "headword_slp1": "jIvati tu vaMSye yuvA", "fold": "jivati tu vansye yuva", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "But when one in a line of descent beginning with a father (and reckoning upwards) is alive, the descendant of a grandson or still lower descendant is called युवन् only.\n\nTerms: युवन्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["जीवति तु वंश्ये युवा ४.१.१६३", "४.१.१६३", "४.१.१६३ जीवति तु वंश्ये युवा"], "synonyms_slp1": ["jIvati tu vaMSye yuvA ४.१.१६३", "४.१.१६३", "४.१.१६३ jIvati tu vaMSye yuvA"]}], "jivikarTe capaRye": [{"id": "jIvikA'rTe cApaRye", "headword": "जीविकाऽर्थे चापण्ये", "headword_slp1": "jIvikA'rTe cApaRye", "fold": "jivikarTe capaRye", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "A similar elision of the affix कन् takes place then also, when the figure is made a means of livelihood, it being presumed, that no traffic is driven thereby.\n\nTerms: कन्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["जीविकाऽर्थे चापण्ये ५.३.९९", "५.३.९९", "५.३.९९ जीविकाऽर्थे चापण्ये"], "synonyms_slp1": ["jIvikA'rTe cApaRye ५.३.९९", "५.३.९९", "५.३.९९ jIvikA'rTe cApaRye"]}]}